+// GalIOS: the level iOS is told. Not the rules' own where they would make iOS lock itself for no real limit:
+// - the case alone tops at HEAVY: its TRAPPING (46 C) and SLEEPING (50 C) are guesses on Samsung's charger scale, and
+//   TRAPPING is Apple's "critical" (iOS shows "iPhone needs to cool down"; the owner's video, 2026-11-14; a later
+//   session ran the whole time at a case of 44-51 C);
+// - the SoC says HEAVY only from 107 C and TRAPPING from 110 C: the S25 Ultra's cores burst to 100-105 C within seconds
+//   of any load and the host's kernel throttles those bursts itself (33 of 39 HEAVY in one session came from them).
+// The battery's rule is told as it is: 50 C at the cell is a real limit. xnuhost's own step (cap) is not changed.
